A nonparametric t test was used for analysis. A p-value of \<0.05 was considered significant.

RESULTS {#sec1-3}
=======

Patient characteristics {#sec2-6}
-----------------------

### Demographic characteristics of subjects {#sec3-1}

Ninety-one female and 55 male patients were included. Average age of patients was 50.6 years (range 20--78 years), with a mean age of 50.8 years for male patients and 48.5 years for female patients (p=0.343).
